00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:52.910
and it's a tremendous consistent producer.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:54.510
So let's give it a sniffy sniff.

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:59.400
On the nose I get a little bit
of oyster shell, very fresh

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:02.520
very sea ocean life.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:07.290
I get a hint of a melon, call
it cantaloupe on the nose.

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:10.600
Little hint of lemon
and lime coming through.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:14.110
So, the classic oysters and cantaloupe

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:16.060
with little Sprite poured on top of it.

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:18.493
Nice nose.

00:05:18.493 --> 00:05:19.350
Let's give it a whirl.

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:44.420
Gorgeous acidity throughout this wine,

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:46.690
a banana peel

00:05:46.690 --> 00:05:50.000
meets granny Smith Apple,

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:50.833
mid palette.

00:05:50.833 --> 00:05:52.880
Huge acid on the finish.

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:54.690
I still am tasting it.

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:56.180
Gorgeous acidity.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:58.490
Now, why is acidity important?

00:05:58.490 --> 00:05:59.880
When I taste this wine,

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:02.880
I know I can use it to cut
through a lot of sea foods;

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:05.260
scallops, oysters, clams.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:06.630
You get into that seafood life.

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:10.460
Even I'm thinking lobster tail in butter,

00:06:10.460 --> 00:06:12.270
but this wine has the acidity cut-through

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:13.103
and match that wine.

00:06:13.103 --> 00:06:15.090
Not be overpowered by the food,

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:18.730
but the wine itself is balanced
and will overpower the wine.

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:21.220
No alcohol in the flavor, beautiful apple.

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:24.430
I really get the granny Apple Smith,

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:27.110
